From 38ac93370767e2b6ce7a7dc503af738938536727 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corios00 <52224974+Corios00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:17:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The client's world API wall pays down eight more crossings

Patch 0097 made crossings into methods on types already published; this does it for eight of
the leaks the series' own patches (0003 to 0087) left in the wall's table, with the same values
and the same arithmetic. No behaviour changes.

- `RigPose::striking_link` and `RigPose::retarget_from` replace `rig_anim::striking_link`,
  `Bones`, `map_bones` and `retarget`: the swing trail and the donor-clip retarget no longer
  assemble a skeleton's parents, rest links and key bones themselves.
- The planted-feet pass reads the ground through `TerrainHeights::under` (published) instead of
  `terrain_stream::terrain_height_under` with the streamer and tiles it held; both resources
  stay optional, so an app with no world still misses every column.
- `WorldPick::ray_posed_mesh` and `ray_mesh_bounds` replace the two free functions the hover
  pick named.
- `WorldDecal::spawn_ground_fx` replaces `ground_fx::spawn_ground_fx_decal`.

Kept, with the reason in the test's comment: the rest are ECS types a game system names in its
own signature or query (components, resources, messages, sets, SystemParams), or items several
game modules name at once (`mesh_tag`, `finalize_rig_worlds`, the pick-part markers,
`PickParts` and `cast_pick_ray_inflated`, the fog override).

World API wall: 121 to 113 (the table's rows go with the crossings).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
